  "answer_text": "In *The Vampire Diaries*, Elena's transformation into a vampire is a major turning point in the series. Here's a full breakdown:\n\n### When Does Elena Turn?\n\nElena Gilbert begins her transformation in **Season 3, Episode 22** \u2014 the finale titled **\"The Departed\"** \u2014 when she drowns after being in a car accident with Matt Donovan.\n\nUnbeknownst to everyone involved, Elena had vampire blood in her system when she died, as Dr. Meredith Fell had injected it into her to save her from fatal injuries inflicted by Klaus.\n\nShe officially **transitions into a vampire** in the **first episode of Season 4**, titled **\"Growing Pains.\"**\n\n### How Does It Happen?\n\nRebekah deliberately causes Matt's vehicle to crash, making the car swerve off Wickery Bridge and plunge into the water below. Although a distraught Stefan arrives on time to save them, Elena urges him to save Matt first \u2014 and by the time Stefan pulls Elena out of the water, she breathes her last.\n\nThe regenerative vampire blood in her bloodstream prevents her from truly dying, causing her to return as a vampire in Season 4, Episode 1, \"Growing Pains.\"\n\n### Was It Intentional?\n\nElena became a vampire despite never wanting to be one. To complete her transformation, Elena must ingest human blood, but she tries her utmost to do this without taking a life.\n\n### Does She Stay a Vampire?\n\nElena woke up as a vampire in Season 3, Episode 22, \"The Departed,\" and remained a vampire for all of Seasons 4, 5, and 6, only getting cured back into a human at the end of Season 6.",
